{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MYZ6PqARinyTwRJiV6TQgS","type":"tool_result","content":"D1 supports three jurisdictions: **eu** (the European Union), **fedramp** (FedRAMP-compliant data centers), and **us** (the United States). So yes, \"us\" is supported.\n\nTo create a database with a jurisdiction using Wrangler, pass the `--jurisdiction` flag:\n\n```sh\nnpx wrangler@latest d1 create <DATABASE_NAME> --jurisdiction=<JURISDICTION>\n```\n\nFor example, `npx wrangler@latest d1 create db-with-jurisdiction --jurisdiction=eu`. Jurisdictions can only be set when you create a database, not added or changed later."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed419c7b-2f33-4a49-81b2-5dd8939e48ab","uuid":"ed237dd4-1dd2-473a-8819-865054b0a361","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:17:50.490Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":7607,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"D1 supports three jurisdictions: **eu** (the European Union), **fedramp** (FedRAMP-compliant data centers), and **us** (the United States). So yes, \"us\" is supported.\n\nTo create a database with a jurisdiction using Wrangler, pass the `--jurisdiction` flag:\n\n```sh\nnpx wrangler@latest d1 create <DATABASE_NAME> --jurisdiction=<JURISDICTION>\n```\n\nFor example, `npx wrangler@latest d1 create db-with-jurisdiction --jurisdiction=eu`. Jurisdictions can only be set when you create a database, not added or changed later.","durationMs":2548,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/configuration/data-location/"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MYZ6PqARinyTwRJiV6TQgS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpkos1QjH4GTQMWGTYPJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the `--jurisdiction` flag when you create the database:\n\n```sh\nnpx wrangler@latest d1 create my-database --jurisdiction=us\n```\n\nThis keeps the database's data inside the United States. D1 also supports `eu` and `fedramp` as jurisdictions. You can only set the jurisdiction when you create the database, so it can't be added or changed later. To move an existing database, you'd have to create a new one with the jurisdiction and migrate your data into it.\n\nSource: [Cloudflare D1 – Data location](https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/configuration/data-location/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":4145,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530},"output_tokens":199,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed419c7b-2f33-4a49-81b2-5dd8939e48ab","uuid":"50636731-43e4-4ecf-8163-e91e0cb169dc","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:17:53.194Z","request_id":"req_011Cfpkorm2c5GoK3vZnZnhg"}
